Third-Party Notices
===============================================================================

This project includes verbatim copies of prompt text from
**oh-my-pi** (also called "omp"), a third-party agent harness.
Upstream: <https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi>

Files affected
--------------

The following files in this repository are verbatim copies of
upstream oh-my-pi files, byte-for-byte:

  crates/prompts/prompts/agents/*.md
    (8 role profiles: task, scout, librarian, reviewer, designer,
     init, security-reviewer, frontmatter)

  crates/prompts/prompts/system/*.md
    (69 system prompt fragments, lexicographic)

  crates/prompts/prompts/system/personalities/*.md
    (3 personality fragments)

These are embedded into the `prompts` crate as Rust constants
through `include_str!`. See `crates/prompts/src/agents.rs` and
`crates/prompts/src/system.rs` for the binding code.

Source pin
----------

Upstream commit: `969a94c1eeccb1b7528cd5621934bca1908ab622`
Upstream branch: `main`
Upstream path:    `packages/coding-agent/src/prompts/`
Captured:         2026-09-04

To re-sync: `cp -v` the upstream files from the desired commit
into the matching `crates/prompts/prompts/` paths, then update the
commit SHA in this file. The `every_system_md_has_a_constant`
test in `crates/prompts/src/system.rs` will fail if a fragment is
added upstream without adding the corresponding constant (and
`include_str!` will fail to compile if a fragment is deleted
upstream without removing its constant).

